---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const credits = [
  ['Background removal model', 'ISNet (general-use weights), as distributed in the @imgly/background-removal-data package, version pinned at build time. Delivered as 11 pieces with a SHA-256 list; the browser checks every piece, and the whole file, before the model runs', 'Apache License 2.0 for the weights; the package data itself states MIT. The model file is used directly through our own runtime code; the @imgly wrapper library is not shipped.'],
  ['Background removal runtime', 'onnxruntime-web 1.31.1', 'MIT License'],
  ['PDF engine', '@cantoo/pdf-lib 2.11.1 (the fork\'s own addition to the library includes its standard security handler: AES-256 encryption and password decryption, which the Protect and Unlock tools run)', 'MIT License'],
  ['PDF page renderer (Read a scan)', 'PDF.js 6.5.438 (pdf.min.mjs and its worker, self-hosted)', 'Apache License 2.0'],
  ['Scan reading engine (OCR)', 'Tesseract.js 7 with the Tesseract LSTM core (WebAssembly, self-hosted) and English, Spanish and Portuguese trained data', 'Apache License 2.0'],
  ['Image codecs', '@jsquash/jpeg 1.6.0 (mozjpeg), @jsquash/webp 1.5.0, @jsquash/png 3.1.1, @jsquash/resize 2.1.1', 'Apache License 2.0 / BSD family, per package'],
  ['HEIC photo reader', 'libheif 1.23.5 with the libde265 decoder, as the libheif-js 1.23.5 WebAssembly build. It runs the HEIC to JPG tool and reads HEIC photos on the other image tools. The section below carries its full notice.', 'GNU Lesser General Public License 3.0 (LGPL-3.0)'],
  ['ZIP packing (batch tools)', 'JSZip 3.10.1', 'MIT License'],
  ['Site frame', 'Astro 5', 'MIT License'],
  ['Styling', 'Tailwind CSS 4', 'MIT License'],
];
---

<Base title="Credits and licences · Benchzy" description="Every engine, model and library Benchzy runs, with its licence. The tools are open-source programs loaded from this site into your browser.">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-4">
    <section class="mt-8">
      <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-accent-deep">Standing page · under the counter</p>
      <h1 class="font-display text-4xl font-black mt-2">Credits and licences</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-lg leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
        Benchzy's tools are open-source programs. They load from this site into your browser and do
        their work there. This page names each one and the licence it ships under. It is kept
        current as engines are pinned or replaced.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-8 grid gap-4">
      {credits.map(([name, what, licence]) => (
        <article class="ticket-soft p-5">
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold">{name}</h2>
          <dl class="mt-2">
            <div class="spec-row"><dt>what runs</dt><dd>{what}</dd></div>
            <div class="spec-row"><dt>licence</dt><dd>{licence}</dd></div>
          </dl>
        </article>
      ))}
    </section>

    <section class="ticket mt-10 p-6">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold">The HEIC reader and the LGPL</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
        The HEIC photo reader is <strong>libheif</strong> (copyright struktur AG, Dirk Farin
        and contributors) with the <strong>libde265</strong> decoder inside it, shipped here
        as the libheif-js 1.23.5 WebAssembly build. Both libraries are free software under
        the <strong>GNU Lesser General Public License, version 3</strong>. The licence text
        is on this site at
        <a class="underline underline-offset-4" href="/heif/LICENSE">/heif/LICENSE</a>,
        exactly as it ships with the library, and the GNU General Public License version 3
        it incorporates is at
        <a class="underline underline-offset-4" href="/heif/GPL-3.0.txt">/heif/GPL-3.0.txt</a>.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
        The library is used <strong>unmodified</strong>, and it is served as its own files
        (<span class="font-mono text-sm">/heif/libheif.js</span> and
        <span class="font-mono text-sm">/heif/libheif.wasm</span>), loaded only when a HEIC
        photo actually arrives, never combined into this site's own code. Because it stays
        a separate file at its own address, you can replace it with your own build of the
        same library and the pages will use yours: that separateness is the point of the
        licence, and we keep it deliberately.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
        The source code for the exact build that runs here: the packaging at
        <a class="underline underline-offset-4" href="https://github.com/catdad-experiments/libheif-js" rel="noopener">github.com/catdad-experiments/libheif-js</a> (version 1.23.5),
        and the libraries themselves at
        <a class="underline underline-offset-4" href="https://github.com/strukturag/libheif" rel="noopener">github.com/strukturag/libheif</a> and
        <a class="underline underline-offset-4" href="https://github.com/strukturag/libde265" rel="noopener">github.com/strukturag/libde265</a>.
        Nothing on this site limits your rights in the library itself.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="ticket mt-10 p-6">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold">Saved on your device</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
        A small service worker (our own code, part of this site) keeps the pages and program
        files your browser has already loaded, so a returning visit does not download the big
        engines again, and a page you have visited can open without a connection. It caches
        program files only. It never sees your files: jobs run in page memory and no request
        carries them.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="ticket mt-10 p-6 mb-4">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold">What is not here</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
        No engine on this page receives your files. There is no upload endpoint, no account system
        and no job counter in the code. If a future tool ever needs a server, this page and the
        tool's own page will say so in plain words before it ships.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
